WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:06.391
After the Ladies' Aid meeting, Pollyanna needed a break.

2
00:00:06.392 --> 00:00:10.470
She didn't want to think about her next conversation with Jimmy.

3
00:00:10.471 --> 00:00:17.139
"I don't have to be home until half past five," she said, heading toward Pendleton Hill.

4
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:24.478
"It'll be so much nicer to walk home through Pendleton Woods."

5
00:00:24.479 --> 00:00:30.222
The woods seemed lovelier than usual to Pollyanna.

6
00:00:30.223 --> 00:00:35.633
For a few minutes, she was able to forget that none of the ladies had wanted Jimmy.

7
00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:40.300
Suddenly a barking dog came dashing down the path toward her.

8
00:00:40.301 --> 00:00:44.226
"Hello, doggie! You belong to Mr. Pendleton!"

9
00:00:44.227 --> 00:00:51.175
Pollyanna waited eagerly for the man to appear, but he did not. "Where is he?"

10
00:00:51.176 --> 00:01:00.857
Meanwhile the dog was acting strangely, giving short barks of alarm and running back and forth.

11
00:01:00.858 --> 00:01:07.415
Pollyanna followed it down a path that branched off to one side.

12
00:01:07.416 --> 00:01:17.006
"Oh, no!" Pollyanna exclaimed, spotting a man lying motionless at the foot of a rocky ledge.

13
00:01:17.007 --> 00:01:21.520
A dead branch cracked sharply under her foot, and the man turned his head toward her.

14
00:01:21.521 --> 00:01:26.248
With a cry of dismay, Pollyanna ran to his side.

15
00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:30.358
"Mr. Pendleton! Are you hurt?"

16
00:01:30.359 --> 00:01:37.066
"No, I'm just taking a nap in the woods," he snapped sarcastically but quickly apologized.

17
00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:43.809
"I beg your pardon, child. It's just this leg of mine." Mr. Pendleton paused.

18
00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:49.918
With some difficulty, he fished a key from his pants pocket and held it out to Pollyanna.

19
00:01:49.919 --> 00:01:52.879
"At the end of this path is my house.

20
00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.981
This key will unlock the side door.

21
00:01:57.982 --> 00:02:01.894
When you get inside, go straight down the hall to the library.

22
00:02:01.895 --> 00:02:05.310
On the desk in the middle of the room, you'll find a telephone.

23
00:02:05.311 --> 00:02:08.117
Do you know how to use a telephone?"

24
00:02:08.118 --> 00:02:11.395
"Oh, yes, sir! Once when Aunt Polly—"

25
00:02:11.396 --> 00:02:13.844
"Never mind Aunt Polly now."

26
00:02:13.845 --> 00:02:18.507
Mr. Pendleton scowled as he struggled to get comfortable.

27
00:02:18.508 --> 00:02:23.927
"Look for Dr. Thomas Chilton's phone number in the address book that you'll find somewhere on the desk.

28
00:02:23.928 --> 00:02:27.196
You know what an address book is, right?"

29
00:02:27.197 --> 00:02:33.514
"Of course! I just love Aunt Polly's! There are so many names, and—"

30
00:02:33.515 --> 00:02:40.202
"Tell Dr. Chilton that John Pendleton is at the foot of Little Eagle Ledge in Pendleton Woods.

31
00:02:40.203 --> 00:02:45.800
Tell him to come at once with a stretcher and two men because I've broken my leg."

32
00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:52.815
"A broken leg? Oh, Mr. Pendleton, how awful!" Pollyanna shuddered.

33
00:02:52.816 --> 00:02:56.573
"Is there anything I can do to help?"

34
00:02:56.574 --> 00:03:01.817
"Yes, you can stop talking and do what I asked!"

35
00:03:01.818 --> 00:03:05.217
Mr. Pendleton moaned in pain.

36
00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:11.530
With a stifled sob, Pollyanna ran off to get help.

37
00:03:11.531 --> 00:03:17.131
It wasn't long before she reached his massive, gray stone house.

38
00:03:17.132 --> 00:03:21.044
She sped across the neglected lawn to the side entrance.

39
00:03:21.045 --> 00:03:26.288
Pollyanna unlocked the heavy, carved door with the key.

40
00:03:26.289 --> 00:03:31.948
Pollyanna knew she should hurry, but she paused in the hall and glanced around.

41
00:03:31.949 --> 00:03:37.387
This was John Pendleton's house, which he never allowed anyone to visit.

42
00:03:37.388 --> 00:03:44.485
Yet he expected Pollyanna to enter the dark, spooky place to help him.

43
00:03:44.486 --> 00:03:52.143
"Who knows what's behind all those doors?" Pollyanna said, frightening herself.

44
00:03:52.144 --> 00:04:00.009
Taking a deep breath, she entered the library.

45
00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:03.665
Books and papers were strewn across the desk and floor.

46
00:04:03.666 --> 00:04:07.090
Everything was covered with dust.

47
00:04:07.091 --> 00:04:13.408
Pollyanna spotted the telephone on the desk, but she had to hunt for the address book.

48
00:04:13.409 --> 00:04:19.902
With shaking hands, Pollyanna turned the pages until she found Dr. Chilton's phone number.

49
00:04:19.903 --> 00:04:26.239
When he answered the phone, she delivered her message and hung up.

50
00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.247
Pollyanna ran back to the woods and sat beside Mr. Pendleton.

51
00:04:30.248 --> 00:04:35.210
"That was quick," he said. "Couldn't you get in?"

52
00:04:35.211 --> 00:04:40.511
"Of course I could! I want to stay with you until Dr. Chilton arrives."

53
00:04:40.512 --> 00:04:44.754
"You could find a nicer person to spend time with than me."

54
00:04:44.755 --> 00:04:48.042
"You mean because you're so grumpy?"

55
00:04:48.043 --> 00:04:53.361
He smiled slightly at her directness. "Yes."

56
00:04:53.362 --> 00:04:57.940
"Oh, you're only grumpy on the outside," Pollyanna said.

57
00:04:57.941 --> 00:05:05.130
"Animals always know who's a good, kind person, and your dog is staying right next to you."

58
00:05:05.131 --> 00:05:09.783
Mr. Pendleton reached out and laid a hand on the dog's head.

59
00:05:09.784 --> 00:05:14.274
At last the dog pricked up its ears and barked.

60
00:05:14.275 --> 00:05:19.176
Pollyanna looked up as Dr. Chilton arrived with two men and a stretcher.

61
00:05:19.177 --> 00:05:27.349
"I couldn't fix Mr. Pendleton's leg," Pollyanna said to Dr. Chilton, "but I'm glad I found him."

62
00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:35.853
"So am I," Dr. Chilton said, and he turned his attention to the injured man.

